// WHAT RClickAutoTrade IS AND WHY THE LEVER CAN CALL IT. It is the path a player's right-click / drag takes
// (read-shops 2a). Its first three acts are `this->getInventory()` (vtable +0x70), `getSection(sectionName)`
// and `getItem(x, y)`: THE ITEM IS NAMED BY A CELL, not by the mouse, so a lever that knows the cell can make
// the same call the player makes. It then asks `isTradingForMoney(this, sendingTo)`, prices the item with the
// SAME `getValueAll` virtual buyItem uses, checks the destination's money, moves the item, and settles with
// `Inventory::takeMoney(dst, +price)` / `takeMoney(src, -price)` (read-prices 2a).
// WHAT IT PRODUCES THAT buyItem DOES NOT: the removal rings on THE SOURCE WINDOW'S OWN SECTION. With the
// shop's facade as the source that is the facade removal `kOwnShopFacade` exists to drop - review-p6v
// HIGH-1's whole point, and the event no `buytest` had ever produced.
// THE RETURN IS A TradeResult BY VALUE: a class with a constructor, so MSVC returns it through a hidden
// pointer passed as the SECOND argument and hands the same pointer back in RAX. build/decomp_713150.txt and
// build/decomp_713d60.txt (RClickAutoTradeAll, which calls it) both show exactly that shape.
