         /* ================= B9 (design-e46-store 2.5 / 2.6): THE WRITER LADDER =================
            READ THE IDENTITY FIRST: entered == r1NotLoadedHere + r2SoleLoaded + r3TieLower + r3TieHigher +
            r4Refused + r3NoAnswer (M2; M2-b: r4Refused also counts a tie refused INSIDE the grace for want of a slot), separately for boxes, for restocks and for doors (B9-b, review-b9 M-2 - doors used to
            be added into the box bucket). It does not balance only if an exit was added
            without a counter. `entered` MUST READ 0 on both games in a clean run with the notebook up - the
            ladder is entered only when the area picture is not fresh, so a non-zero here in a healthy run
            says the picture verdict is wrong, not that the ladder is.
            THE Spans BRACKET IS NOT PART OF THE IDENTITY. r2PeerUnknown = the other game had not reported
            its loaded set, so the tie-break decided (r3ByRole is RETIRED by M2-b: since M2 it always equalled
            r3NoAnswer, so the field is gone from the readout rather than duplicated); r4GracePasses = the notebook was down and the grace
            had not yet run out. */
