// ==== p105h (P105 build 1, .modding/investigations/p105-boxmove-cursor-design-2026-10-02.md 10 / 15.1 / 15.2): TEST LEVERS ====
/* `cursortest open <boxKey> | close | pick <container> <section> <x> <y> [all] | drop <container> <section> <x> <y> | back | list`
   and `boxmove <boxKey> <section> <fx> <fy> <tx> <ty> [n]`. TEST-ONLY: nothing here runs unless a command names it, and none of it
   changes what a player's game does. MAIN THREAD (the command channel). Every call writes ONE `[ITEMS] p105 cursortest ...` /
   `[ITEMS] p105 boxmove ...` line, refusals included.
   <container>: a box key as boxlist prints it (key=...), `me` (this game's lowest-uid own player-faction character - the one the
   loot open shows beside the box, boxopen's opener) or `peer` (the other game's character with the lowest uid, itemtake's rule).
   pick / drop act on a container whose window is OPEN (cursortest open opens a box through boxopen's road, the engine's loot open,
   which also shows `me`); a container with no window is refused.

   HOW THE ENGINE'S OWN PICKUP IS AIMED (15.1, Read): InventoryGUI::pickupItemToMouse(window, section by value) takes NO square - it
   truncates the two mouse-position floats the GUI keeps, subtracts the section grid's left / top (the window's section map at +0x60,
   std::map keyed by the section name; the mapped object's first pointer, whose +0x30 / +0x34 are the grid's screen left / top) and
   divides by the slot-size ints. So the lever writes the mouse floats to the CENTRE of the wanted square around the call and puts
   the old values back right after it. One unit or the whole stack are its only answers: the whole stack when the shift-held byte
   (the RClickAllFlag row) is set, so `all` sets it around the call too.
   THOSE FOUR GLOBALS HAVE NO TABLE ROW. They are read out of the pickup's own instructions - each one's RIP-relative operand, at a
   fixed distance from the function entry the table already verifies (GuiPickup) - and every one of those instructions' opcode
   bytes is checked first. The distances and opcodes were read from both executables offline (1.0.65 0x712DD0, 1.0.68 0x7139A0:
   the same distances, the same opcodes; the decoded globals were 0x2132424 / 0x2132428 / 0x2127440 / 0x2127444 on 1.0.65). As a
   check of the method itself, the SAME decode of the pickup's shift-byte test must give the RClickAllFlag row's address, or every
   pick / drop is refused.
   HOW THE DROP IS AIMED (15.2 + the 0x70CB60 read; T808 fix): placeItemFromMouse(window, section by value, point) hands its point
   unchanged to its point-to-square step 0x70CB60 (decomp_714990:94), which subtracts the same grid left / top as the pickup (the
   window's section-map object +0x30 / +0x34), divides by the same slot-size globals (0x2127440 / 0x2127444 on 1.0.65) and clamps
   to the SECTION's own width / height (section +0x30 / +0x34) - decomp_70cb60. It has two arms: whole-number division, or a float
   division ROUNDED TO THE NEAREST whole number (0x9B23E0 is UtilityT::round(float), build/exports_all.txt); the drop takes the
   rounding arm (Inferred: decomp_714990:93 writes 1 into the fifth-argument stack slot just before the call). The point is the
   ITEM's top-left corner, not the pointer, so the square's CENTRE is the wrong aim (x + 0.5 rounds to the next square). The lever
   aims a QUARTER of a square in from the square's top-left pixel (x + 0.25 truncates AND rounds to x), and before calling it
   recomputes the square from that pixel by BOTH arms and the clamp (P105CellOfPixel) and refuses if either is not the wanted
   square. After that, 0x74B380 (decomp_74b380) refuses only when the section's enabled byte +0xD0 is 0 or its type list
   (isLimitedSlotCompatible 0x74B0F0, limitedTo=) refuses the item, and otherwise shifts the square left / up until the item fits
   the grid; the drop then counts what lies under the footprint. That is the lever's PREMISE check: fitsAt + nothing in
   the footprint (ItFitsPod). What the lever cannot check first: the trade check 0x70C6C0 ("gui_notrade") and the cursor-item
   checks that show codes 0x11 / 5 / 7 (decomp_714990:80-260). Each of those refusals puts the item back itself (0x70D000) and
   returns 0. T808's drop was aimed at the top-left pixel (both arms give the square there), so its engine=0 was one of those
   gates, not the aim (Inferred). The drop line reports engine= and where the carried object is afterwards; never ok on 0.
   THE SECTION: the mod's own lookup first (Inventory::getSection by name, as itemtake) - the square check and the item reads use
   that section. The two engine calls themselves take NO section pointer: both take the section NAME as a std::string BY VALUE
   (Read: 0x712DD0 looks the name up in the window's section map; 0x714990 hands it to Inventory::getSection 0x747070 and to the
   same map lookup 0x161D20), which under the x64 ABI is the address of a caller-built string the CALLEE destroys (frees its
   buffer and empties it - decomp_712dd0 :37-42, decomp_714990 :672-679). So the lever builds a real string in its own 0x28-byte slot
   with the mod's std::string::assign - the road store.cpp Pp7AssignEngineStringPod takes into an engine string, and
   ShopFreeByValueStr frees one by: the mod and the engine share one CRT heap - and never touches it after the call. Any length.
   The slot is 0x28 bytes, the same layout as the engine's string (P105StrPod below); the lever refuses if the sizes differ.
   If the call FAULTS the string is left alone (at worst one name's buffer leaks; freeing it could free it twice). */
namespace {
const size_t kP105GuiSecMap  = 0x60;   /* InventoryGUI: the section-name -> grid map (the pickup's `LEA RCX,[RBP+0x60]` before its lookup) */
const size_t kP105MapNodeKey = 0x18;   /* that map's node: the key string (0x161D20 compares the name with node+0x18) */
const size_t kP105MapNodeVal = 0x40;   /* ... and the mapped value (0x161D20 returns node+0x40) */
const size_t kP105GridLeft   = 0x30;   /* the mapped object's first pointer -> +0x30 left, +0x34 top (pickup and 0x70CB60 alike) */
const size_t kP105GridTop    = 0x34;
struct P105StrPod { char buf[16]; unsigned long long size; unsigned long long res; unsigned long long alloc; };   /* this build's (VS2010) std::string, 0x28 bytes: the buffer / heap-pointer union +0, size +0x10, capacity +0x18 (ItStrPodWhy's reads), then the allocator member padded to 8 at +0x20 (store.cpp static_assert 0x28; the section map's node key +0x18 / value +0x40 agree) */
struct P105Globals { float* mouseX; float* mouseY; int* slotW; int* slotH; unsigned char* allFlag; int state; };   /* state 0 unread, 1 ok, -1 refused */
P105Globals g_p105G = { 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 };
int g_p105HaveTown = 0;
int g_p105Town[kTownHandDwords];
long long g_p105Picks = 0, g_p105Drops = 0, g_p105Backs = 0, g_p105Moves = 0, g_p105Refused = 0;
const size_t kP105SecGridW   = 0x30;   /* InventorySection: the width / height 0x70CB60 clamps to and 0x74B380 fits against (decomp_70cb60, decomp_74b380) */
const size_t kP105SecGridH   = 0x34;
const size_t kP105SecEnabled = 0xD0;   /* InventorySection: 0x74B380 refuses every item when this byte is 0 (decomp_74b380) */
std::string g_p105PickWho, g_p105PickSec;   /* the last ok pick's source (container token, section name) and object: the drop's "where is it now" */
void* g_p105PickItem = 0;

/* the target of the RIP-relative operand of the instruction at fn+off, after its opcode bytes are checked. 1 ok, 0 not. */
int P105RipPod(const unsigned char* fn, size_t off, const unsigned char* pre, int preLen, int dispPos, int insLen, void** out)
{
    *out = 0;
    __try
    {
        const unsigned char* ins = fn + off;
        for (int i = 0; i < preLen; ++i) if (ins[i] != pre[i]) return 0;
        const int disp = *(const int*)(ins + dispPos);
        *out = (void*)(ins + insLen + disp);
        return 1;
    }
    __except (EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER) { *out = 0; return 0; }
}
/* the pickup's four globals (and its shift byte, the method's check). 1 resolved, 0 refused (state says why it stays refused). */
int P105GlobalsOk()
{
    if (g_p105G.state != 0) return (g_p105G.state == 1) ? 1 : 0;
    g_p105G.state = -1;
    if (g_base == 0 || kGuiPickupRva == 0 || kRClickAllFlagRva == 0) return 0;
    const unsigned char* fn = (const unsigned char*)(g_base + kGuiPickupRva);
    static const unsigned char kCvtEbx[4] = { 0xF3, 0x0F, 0x2C, 0x1D };         /* cvttss2si ebx, [rip+d]  - mouse y */
    static const unsigned char kCvtR14[5] = { 0xF3, 0x44, 0x0F, 0x2C, 0x35 };   /* cvttss2si r14d, [rip+d] - mouse x */
    static const unsigned char kIdiv[2]   = { 0xF7, 0x3D };                     /* idiv dword [rip+d]      - slot w / h */
    static const unsigned char kCmpB[2]   = { 0x80, 0x3D };                     /* cmp byte [rip+d], 0     - the shift byte */
    void* my = 0; void* mx = 0; void* sw = 0; void* sh = 0; void* af = 0;
    if (P105RipPod(fn, 0xEA, kCvtEbx, 4, 4, 8, &my) == 0 || P105RipPod(fn, 0xF2, kCvtR14, 5, 5, 9, &mx) == 0
        || P105RipPod(fn, 0x114, kIdiv, 2, 2, 6, &sw) == 0 || P105RipPod(fn, 0x123, kIdiv, 2, 2, 6, &sh) == 0
        || P105RipPod(fn, 0x268, kCmpB, 2, 2, 7, &af) == 0) return 0;
    if (af != (void*)(g_base + kRClickAllFlagRva)) return 0;
    g_p105G.mouseX = (float*)mx; g_p105G.mouseY = (float*)my; g_p105G.slotW = (int*)sw; g_p105G.slotH = (int*)sh;
    g_p105G.allFlag = (unsigned char*)af; g_p105G.state = 1;
    return 1;
}
int P105SlotSizePod(int* w, int* h)
{
    __try { *w = *g_p105G.slotW; *h = *g_p105G.slotH; return (*w > 0 && *h > 0) ? 1 : 0; }
    __except (EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER) { return 0; }
}
/* the screen left / top of the window's grid for section `name`: the window's map walked read-only (every node, the map's head as
   the end marker on both sides - no ordering or colour flag is relied on). 1 found, 0 not / faulted. */
int P105GridLeftTopPod(void* gui, const char* name, int* left, int* top)
{
    __try
    {
        const char* const head = *(const char* const*)((const char*)gui + kP105GuiSecMap + 8);
        if (!ItPlaus(head)) return 0;
        const char* stack[64];
        int sp = 0, steps = 0;
        stack[sp++] = *(const char* const*)(head + 8);
        while (sp > 0)
        {
            const char* node = stack[--sp];
            if (node == head || !ItPlaus(node)) continue;
            if (++steps > 256) return 0;
            char key[64];
            if (ItStrPodWhy(node + kP105MapNodeKey, key, (int)sizeof(key)) == 1 && std::strcmp(key, name) == 0)
            {
                const char* val = *(const char* const*)(node + kP105MapNodeVal);
                if (!ItPlaus(val)) return 0;
                const char* grid = *(const char* const*)val;
                if (!ItPlaus(grid)) return 0;
                *left = *(const int*)(grid + kP105GridLeft);
                *top = *(const int*)(grid + kP105GridTop);
                return 1;
            }
            if (sp + 2 > 64) return 0;
            stack[sp++] = *(const char* const*)node;            /* left */
            stack[sp++] = *(const char* const*)(node + 0x10);   /* right */
        }
        return 0;
    }
    __except (EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER) { return 0; }
}
/* the engine's pickup at its hooked entry, the mouse floats (and the shift byte for `all`) set around it and put back. 1 called. */
int P105PickPod(void* gui, P105StrPod* s, float px, float py, int all, int* ret)
{
    *ret = -1;
    float ox = 0.0f, oy = 0.0f; unsigned char of = 0; int saved = 0;
    __try
    {
        __try
        {
            ox = *g_p105G.mouseX; oy = *g_p105G.mouseY; of = *g_p105G.allFlag; saved = 1;
            *g_p105G.mouseX = px; *g_p105G.mouseY = py; *g_p105G.allFlag = (unsigned char)(all != 0 ? 1 : 0);
            GuiPickupFn fn = (GuiPickupFn)(g_base + kGuiPickupRva);
            *ret = (int)(unsigned char)fn(gui, (void*)s);
        }
        __finally
        {
            if (saved != 0) { *g_p105G.mouseX = ox; *g_p105G.mouseY = oy; *g_p105G.allFlag = of; }
        }
        return 1;
    }
    __except (EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER) { return 0; }
}
int P105PlacePod(void* gui, P105StrPod* s, int px, int py, int* ret)
{
    *ret = -1;
    __try
    {
        int pt[2]; pt[0] = px; pt[1] = py;
        GuiPlaceFn fn = (GuiPlaceFn)(g_base + kGuiPlaceRva);
        *ret = (int)(unsigned char)fn(gui, (void*)s, (void*)pt);
        return 1;
    }
    __except (EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER) { return 0; }
}
int P105ReturnPod()
{
    __try
    {
        void* holder = *(void* const*)(g_base + kMouseInvPtrRva);
        if (!ItPlaus(holder)) return 0;
        MouseReturnFn fn = (MouseReturnFn)(g_base + kMouseReturnItemRva);
        fn(holder);
        return 1;
    }
    __except (EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER) { return 0; }
}
void P105MakeStr(P105StrPod* s, const std::string& name)
{
    std::memset(s, 0, sizeof(*s));
    s->size = 0; s->res = 15;   /* an empty short string, the state std::string's own constructor leaves */
    ((std::string*)s)->assign(name.c_str(), name.size());   /* the mod's own string code: a heap buffer for 16+ characters */
}
std::string P105ItemDesc(void* item)
{
    if (!ItPlaus(item)) return "empty";
    char sid[96]; sid[0] = 0;
    int q = -1;
    if (ItBaseSidPod(item, sid, (int)sizeof(sid)) == 0) std::strcpy(sid, "?");
    ItIntPod(item, kItemQuantity, &q);
    return std::string(sid) + " x" + N((long long)q);
}
std::vector<std::string> P105Tokens(const std::string& arg)
{
    std::vector<std::string> tok;
    std::string cur;
    for (size_t i = 0; i <= arg.size(); ++i)
    {
        if (i == arg.size() || arg[i] == ' ' || arg[i] == '\t' || arg[i] == '\r' || arg[i] == '\n') { if (!cur.empty()) tok.push_back(cur); cur.clear(); }
        else cur += arg[i];
    }
    return tok;
}
int P105Int(const std::string& s, int lo, int hi, int* out)
{
    if (s.empty() || s.size() > 6) return 0;
    int v = 0;
    for (size_t i = 0; i < s.size(); ++i) { if (s[i] < '0' || s[i] > '9') return 0; v = v * 10 + (s[i] - '0'); }
    if (v < lo || v > hi) return 0;
    *out = v; return 1;
}
/* <container> -> its inventory; *desc names it for the line. 0 = not found (desc says why). */
::Inventory* P105Container(const std::string& who, std::string* desc)
{
    if (!ItPlaus(coop::GameWorldPtr())) { *desc = "no GameWorld"; return 0; }
    if (who == "me")
    {
        ::Character* c = ItBoxOpenOpener();
        if (c == 0) { *desc = "no player-faction character with a uid this game owns"; return 0; }
        *desc = "this game's character uid " + N((long long)FindSpawnedUid(c));
        return ItInventoryOf(c);
    }
    if (who == "peer")
    {
        const GameHashSet< ::Character*>::type& all = coop::GameWorldPtr()->activeCharacters();
        if (all.size() > 20000) { *desc = "the character update list is implausible"; return 0; }
        ::Character* ghost = 0;
        unsigned int gu = 0;
        for (GameHashSet< ::Character*>::type::const_iterator it = all.begin(); it != all.end(); ++it)
        {
            ::Character* c = *it;
            if (!ItObj(c)) continue;
            void* pf = 0;
            const unsigned int pu = FindSpawnedUid(c);
            if (pu != 0 && !net::IsUidMine(pu) && ItFactionPod(c, &pf) != 0 && IsStandInFaction((::Faction*)pf) && (ghost == 0 || pu < gu))
            { ghost = c; gu = pu; }
        }
        if (ghost == 0) { *desc = "no character of the other game is loaded here"; return 0; }
        *desc = "the other game's character uid " + N((long long)gu);
        return ItInventoryOf(ghost);
    }
    void* b = ItBoxResolve(who.c_str());
    if (b == 0) { *desc = "no loaded box has the key " + who; return 0; }
    *desc = "box '" + who + "' (verdict " + N((long long)ItBoxMoveVerdict(b, who)) + ")";
    return ItBoxInventory(b);
}
/* the open window showing `inv`, or 0 (the P7d round trip: the window must name the same inventory back) */
void* P105WindowOf(::Inventory* inv)
{
    void* gui = 0;
    if (inv == 0 || ItInventoryGuiPod(inv, &gui) == 0 || gui == 0) return 0;
    return (ItSameWindow(gui, inv) != 0) ? gui : 0;
}
/* 0x70CB60's pixel-to-square for ONE axis, both arms (decomp_70cb60): (p - origin) / slot as whole-number division (C and the
   engine's idiv both truncate toward zero), or as a float division rounded to the nearest whole number (UtilityT::round; halves
   away from zero is Inferred - the lever's aim is never near a half), then clamped to 0..cells-1. -1 = no slot size. */
int P105CellOfPixel(int p, int origin, int slot, int cells, int roundArm)
{
    if (slot <= 0 || cells <= 0) return -1;
    int c = 0;
    if (roundArm == 0) c = (p - origin) / slot;
    else
    {
        const float v = (float)(p - origin) / (float)slot;
        c = (v >= 0.0f) ? (int)(v + 0.5f) : -(int)(-v + 0.5f);
    }
    if (c > cells - 1) c = cells - 1;
    if (c < 0) c = 0;
    return c;
}
/* THE DROP'S AIM CHECK: the pixel converted back by both arms of 0x70CB60 with the section's own clamp. "" = both give (x,y);
   otherwise the reason. *fields gets the inputs and both answers for the line. */
std::string P105AimCheck(::InventorySection* sec, int px, int py, int left, int top, int sw, int sh, int x, int y, std::string* fields)
{
    int gw = 0, gh = 0;
    *fields = " grid=" + N(left) + "," + N(top) + " slot=" + N(sw) + "x" + N(sh);
    if (ItIntPod(sec, kP105SecGridW, &gw) == 0 || ItIntPod(sec, kP105SecGridH, &gh) == 0 || gw <= 0 || gh <= 0)
        return "the section's own width / height (+0x30 / +0x34, 0x70CB60's clamp) did not read";
    const int tx = P105CellOfPixel(px, left, sw, gw, 0), ty = P105CellOfPixel(py, top, sh, gh, 0);
    const int rx = P105CellOfPixel(px, left, sw, gw, 1), ry = P105CellOfPixel(py, top, sh, gh, 1);
    *fields += " gridWxH=" + N(gw) + "x" + N(gh) + " recheck trunc=" + N(tx) + "," + N(ty) + " round=" + N(rx) + "," + N(ry);
    if (tx != x || ty != y || rx != x || ry != y) return "the pixel does not convert back to the wanted square";
    return "";
}
/* THE FIXTURE CHECK's fields for (sec, item, x, y): the section's type list and sizes (ItSectionLimitFields: secWxH itemWxH
   limitedTo=), its enabled byte, the square's occupant, and (askFits) the mod's own cell test ItFitsPod - fitsAt (enabled,
   type list, fits the grid) + nothing in the footprint: 1 yes, 0 no, -1 faulted. */
std::string P105Premise(::InventorySection* sec, void* item, int x, int y, int askFits, int* fits)
{
    int en = -1;
    if (ItBytePod(sec, kP105SecEnabled, &en) == 0) en = -1;
    void* at = 0;
    const int asked = ItGetAtPod(sec, x, y, &at);
    *fits = -2;
    if (askFits != 0) *fits = ItFitsPod(sec, item, x, y);
    return ItSectionLimitFields(sec, item) + " enabled=" + N(en) + " square="
         + (asked == 0 ? std::string("unreadable") : (at == 0 ? std::string("free") : "occupied by " + P105ItemDesc(at)))
         + (askFits != 0 ? " fits=" + N(*fits) : std::string());
}
/* where the carried object is now: on the cursor, in the target section (*tx,*ty), back in the last pick's source square, or
   elsewhere. Pointer compares only (a merge destroys the object; it is never read). */
std::string P105WhereIs(void* item, void* cursor, ::InventorySection* target, int* tx, int* ty)
{
    *tx = -1; *ty = -1;
    if (item == 0) return "unknown (no object)";
    if (cursor == item) return "on the cursor";
    ItSlotOfInSection(target, (::Item*)item, tx, ty);
    if (*tx >= 0) return "in the target section at " + N(*tx) + "," + N(*ty);
    if (item == g_p105PickItem && !g_p105PickWho.empty())
    {
        std::string d;
        ::Inventory* inv = P105Container(g_p105PickWho, &d);
        ::InventorySection* ps = (inv != 0) ? inv->getSection(g_p105PickSec) : 0;
        int sx = -1, sy = -1;
        if (ItObj(ps)) ItSlotOfInSection(ps, (::Item*)item, &sx, &sy);
        if (sx >= 0) return "back at the pick's source " + g_p105PickWho + " " + g_p105PickSec + " " + N(sx) + "," + N(sy);
        return "elsewhere (not on the cursor, not in the target section, not in the pick's source " + g_p105PickWho + " " + g_p105PickSec + ")";
    }
    return "elsewhere (not on the cursor, not in the target section; no pick of this object recorded)";
}
/* the shared front half of pick / drop: container, its open window, the named section, the square, the grid's left / top */
std::string P105Aim(const std::vector<std::string>& tok, const char* verb, ::Inventory** inv, void** gui, ::InventorySection** sec,
                    int* x, int* y, int* left, int* top, int* sw, int* sh, std::string* desc)
{
    if (P105GlobalsOk() == 0)
        return std::string("error cursortest ") + verb + ": the pickup's mouse / slot globals could not be read from its code (opcode check or the"
               " RClickAllFlag cross-check failed) - nothing called";
    if (kGuiPlaceRva == 0 || kMouseInvPtrRva == 0) return std::string("error cursortest ") + verb + ": the GUI drop / cursor rows are not bound";
    if (sizeof(std::string) != 0x28 || sizeof(P105StrPod) != 0x28) return std::string("error cursortest ") + verb + ": this build's std::string or the lever's string slot is not the engine's 0x28-byte layout - nothing called";
    if (P105Int(tok[3], 0, 999, x) == 0 || P105Int(tok[4], 0, 999, y) == 0) return std::string("error cursortest ") + verb + ": x and y must be whole numbers 0..999";
    *inv = P105Container(tok[1], desc);
    if (*inv == 0) return std::string("error cursortest ") + verb + ": " + *desc;
    *gui = P105WindowOf(*inv);
    if (*gui == 0) return std::string("error cursortest ") + verb + ": no open window shows " + *desc + " (cursortest open <boxKey> first)";
    *sec = (*inv)->getSection(tok[2]);
    if (!ItObj(*sec)) return std::string("error cursortest ") + verb + ": " + *desc + " has no section called '" + tok[2] + "'";
    if (ItSlotInSectionWhy(*sec, *x, *y) != 1) return std::string("error cursortest ") + verb + ": " + tok[2] + " has no square " + N((long long)*x) + "," + N((long long)*y);
    if (P105GridLeftTopPod(*gui, tok[2].c_str(), left, top) == 0) return std::string("error cursortest ") + verb + ": the window's grid for '" + tok[2] + "' was not found in its section map";
    if (P105SlotSizePod(sw, sh) == 0) return std::string("error cursortest ") + verb + ": the slot size could not be read";
    return "";
}
/* T818 (owner 352 a): THE ENGINE'S OWN REFUSAL REASON. Every message placeItemFromMouse 0x714990 shows on a refusal goes through ONE
   function, the refusal-message function (table row TradeResultMessage: 0x70EC10 on 1.0.65, 0x70F7E0 on 1.0.68), handed a pointer
   to the code (decomp_70ec10's switch). detour_p105Msg is installed only the FIRST time `cursortest drop` reaches its engine call
   (P105InstallMsgHook, main thread, tried once - success or failure is remembered), so a game that never uses the lever has no
   extra hook. It ALWAYS runs the original; it only remembers the code while `cursortest drop` has armed it around its one engine
   call (main thread). Nothing a player sees changes.
   The drop's SILENT refusals show no message (decomp_714990): a section named "out" (:94-107), the square shift failing on an item
   the section's type list takes (:148-155), two or more items under the footprint (:186 / :641), the section's item-count cap
   0x719B80 when nothing is under it (:189-191: section +0xA8 > 0 and +0xA8 <= its item count (+0x48 - +0x40) / 16), and the
   trade-only test 0x7146C0 (:330). So the drop line also prints cap / count / the section type (+0xB8: a type other than 7 asks the
   can't-wear test, :164 - code 5). */
typedef void (*P105MsgFn)(int* result);
P105MsgFn orig_p105Msg = 0;
volatile LONG g_p105MsgArm = 0;
int g_p105MsgCode = 0;    /* the last code shown while armed */
int g_p105MsgCount = 0;   /* how many shown while armed */
int g_p105MsgHook = 0;    /* 0 = not tried yet, 1 = installed, -1 = not installable (no table row, or AddHook failed) - tried once */
void detour_p105Msg(int* result)
{
    if (g_p105MsgArm != 0)
    {
        int c = -1;
        __try { if (result != 0) c = *result; }
        __except (EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER) { c = -2; }
        g_p105MsgCode = c;
        ++g_p105MsgCount;
    }
    orig_p105Msg(result);
}
/* our own short names for the engine's message codes (decomp_70ec10) */
const char* P105ReasonText(int c)
{
    switch (c)
    {
    case 1: return "out-of-trading-range";
    case 2: return "no-room";
    case 3: return "buyer-cannot-afford";
    case 4: return "shopkeeper-cannot-afford";
    case 5: return "cannot-wear";
    case 6: return "invalid-container-type";
    case 7: return "item-locked-in-place";
    case 8: return "caught-stealing";
    case 9: return "caught-selling-stolen";
    case 0xC: return "not-for-sale";
    case 0xD: return "target-conscious";
    case 0xE: return "smugglers-buy-illegal-only";
    case 0xF: return "attempted-smuggling";
    case 0x10: return "uniform-refused";
    case 0x11: return "container-must-be-empty";
    default: return "unknown-code";
    }
}
/* T818 review (P105 lazy reason hook: installed once): the reason hook, installed the FIRST time `cursortest drop` reaches its engine call (MAIN THREAD),
   never at startup; tried once, the result remembered in g_p105MsgHook. Logs its one install line then. */
void P105InstallMsgHook()
{
    if (g_p105MsgHook != 0) return;
    if (g_base == 0 || kTradeResultMessageRva == 0)
    {
        g_p105MsgHook = -1;
        DebugLog("[ITEMS] p105 reason hook NOT installed: no TradeResultMessage row - cursortest drop prints engineReason=unhooked");
        return;
    }
    const coop::HookStatus h = coop::AddHook((void*)(g_base + kTradeResultMessageRva), (void*)&detour_p105Msg, (void**)&orig_p105Msg);
    g_p105MsgHook = (h == coop::SUCCESS) ? 1 : -1;
    if (g_p105MsgHook == 1) DebugLog("[ITEMS] hook installed (first cursortest drop): the refusal-message function, TradeResultMessage row (test lever only: remembers the code while cursortest drop is armed)");
    else ErrorLog("[ITEMS] AddHook the refusal-message function (TradeResultMessage row) FAILED - cursortest drop prints engineReason=unhooked");
}
/* The flag the drop hands its range test as the third argument: 0x710B70(target window, the cursor's source window) - decomp_714990
   :80-82. Its address is decoded from the drop's own CALL at fn+0xEA (a jump thunk to 0x710B70 on 1.0.65, 0x711740 on 1.0.68) after
   the 17 bytes before it (fn+0xD9: RDX = MouseInventory +0x68, RCX = the window) and the 9 after it are checked - the same bytes at
   the same distances in both executables (read offline), so another build is refused, never called. Then the range test 0x70C6C0 is
   asked AGAIN as the engine asks it: the target window, the source window's slot 0x80 answer, that flag. *flag / *ok: 1 / 0, or -1
   not asked. 0x710B70 is look-up-or-create (not a pure read), so P105GateFields is called only after the drop's aim and premise
   checks passed - right before the engine's own drop, which makes the same two calls at its start. MAIN THREAD. */
typedef char (*P105FlagFn)(void* target, void* source);
int P105StrictPod(void* gui, int* flag, int* ok)
{
    *flag = -1; *ok = -1;
    if (g_base == 0 || kGuiPlaceRva == 0 || kTradeRangeCheckRva == 0 || !ItPlaus(gui)) return 0;
    static const unsigned char kPre[18] = { 0x49, 0x8B, 0x56, 0x68, 0x48, 0x85, 0xD2, 0x75, 0x02, 0xEB, 0xBF, 0x48, 0x8B, 0xFA, 0x49, 0x8B, 0xCF, 0xE8 };
    static const unsigned char kPost[9] = { 0x0F, 0xB6, 0xD8, 0x48, 0x8B, 0x17, 0x48, 0x8B, 0xCF };
    const unsigned char* fn = (const unsigned char*)(g_base + kGuiPlaceRva);
    void* target = 0;
    if (P105RipPod(fn, 0xD9, kPre, 18, 18, 22, &target) == 0 || target == 0) return 0;
    __try
    {
        for (int i = 0; i < 9; ++i) if (fn[0xEF + i] != kPost[i]) return 0;
        void* m = ShopMousePod();
        void* src = (m != 0) ? *(void* const*)((const char*)m + kMouseInvSrcWin) : 0;
        if (!ItPlaus(src)) return 0;
        const char f = ((P105FlagFn)target)(gui, src);
        *flag = (f != 0) ? 1 : 0;
        void* other = (*(ShopVoidGetFn*)(*(const char* const*)src + kVtGuiRangeOther))(src);
        if (!ItPlaus(other)) return 1;
        *ok = (((ShopTradeRangeFn)(g_base + kTradeRangeCheckRva))(gui, other, (char)*flag) != 0) ? 1 : 0;
        return 1;
    }
    __except (EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER) { *flag = -1; *ok = -1; return 0; }
}
/* the target section's silent-gate reads (decomp_719b80, decomp_714990 :164): cap +0xA8, item count (+0x48 - +0x40) / 16, type +0xB8 */
int P105GatePod(void* sec, int* cap, long long* cnt, int* type)
{
    *cap = 0; *cnt = -1; *type = -1;
    __try
    {
        const char* p = (const char*)sec;
        *cap = *(const int*)(p + 0xA8);
        *cnt = (*(const long long*)(p + 0x48) - *(const long long*)(p + 0x40)) >> 4;
        *type = *(const int*)(p + 0xB8);
        return 1;
    }
    __except (EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER) { return 0; }
}
std::string P105GateFields(void* gui, void* sec)
{
    int flag = -1, ok = -1, cap = 0, type = -1;
    long long cnt = -1;
    P105StrictPod(gui, &flag, &ok);
    std::string r = " strictFlag=" + N((long long)flag) + " strictRangeOk=" + N((long long)ok);
    if (P105GatePod(sec, &cap, &cnt, &type) == 0) return r + " cap=unread";
    return r + " cap=" + N((long long)cap) + " count=" + N(cnt) + " capFull=" + N((long long)((cap > 0 && (long long)cap <= cnt) ? 1 : 0))
         + " secType=" + N((long long)type);
}
/* T816 lever premise: the FIRST check of placeItemFromMouse 0x714990 (decomp_714990 :83-90) is the trade-range test 0x70C6C0 (the
   target window, the cursor's source window's owner): ground-plane (x, z) distance squared < 1,000,000, stricter for some flagged
   cases. `other` = the far object, or 0 = the owner (slot 0x80) of the cursor's source window (MouseInventory +0x68). *ok = the
   engine's own answer (1 in range, 0 out, -1 not asked), *d = the distance measured as 0x70C6C0 does (slot 0x80 owner, slot 0x40
   position). Only reads positions and types. MAIN THREAD. */
typedef float* (*P105PosFn)(void* self, void* out);
int P105RangePod(void* gui, void* other, int* ok, float* d)
{
    *ok = -1; *d = -1.0f;
    if (g_base == 0 || kTradeRangeCheckRva == 0 || !ItPlaus(gui)) return 0;
    __try
    {
        void* m = (other == 0) ? ShopMousePod() : 0;
        void* src = (m != 0) ? *(void* const*)((const char*)m + kMouseInvSrcWin) : 0;
        if (other == 0 && ItPlaus(src)) other = (*(ShopVoidGetFn*)(*(const char* const*)src + kVtGuiRangeOther))(src);
        void* own = (*(ShopVoidGetFn*)(*(const char* const*)gui + kVtGuiRangeOther))(gui);
        if (!ItPlaus(other) || !ItPlaus(own)) return 0;
        float a[4] = { 0 }, b[4] = { 0 };
        const float* pa = (*(P105PosFn*)(*(const char* const*)own + 0x40))(own, a);
        const float* pb = (*(P105PosFn*)(*(const char* const*)other + 0x40))(other, b);
        *d = std::sqrt((pa[0] - pb[0]) * (pa[0] - pb[0]) + (pa[2] - pb[2]) * (pa[2] - pb[2]));
        *ok = (((ShopTradeRangeFn)(g_base + kTradeRangeCheckRva))(gui, other, 0) != 0) ? 1 : 0;
        return 1;
    }
    __except (EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER) { *ok = -1; return 0; }
}
/* " range=<d> rangeOk=<1|0>" for a fixture: field (" range=unread" when the question could not be asked) */
std::string P105RangeField(void* gui, void* other, int* ok)
{
    float d = -1.0f;
    if (P105RangePod(gui, other, ok, &d) == 0 || *ok < 0) return " range=unread";
    return " range=" + N((long long)(d + 0.5f)) + " rangeOk=" + N((long long)*ok) + " (limit 1000)";
}
std::string P105CursorBody(const std::string& arg)
{
    const std::vector<std::string> tok = P105Tokens(arg);
    const std::string usage = "error cursortest usage: cursortest open <boxKey> | close | pick <boxKey|me|peer> <section> <x> <y> [all]"
                              " | drop <boxKey|me|peer> <section> <x> <y>|free | back | list | square <boxKey|me|peer> <section> <x> <y>";
    if (tok.empty()) return usage;
    if (g_base == 0) return "error cursortest: not installed";
    if (ItOnMainThread() == 0) return "error cursortest: not on the main thread";
    if (StoreTearingDown() != 0) return "error cursortest: the engine is tearing the world down - try again";
    const std::string& v = tok[0];
    void* const cur0 = ItHeldLive();
    if (v == "list")
    {
        if (tok.size() != 1) return usage;
        return "ok cursortest list cursor=" + P105ItemDesc(cur0) + " heldSlot=" + N((long long)::InterlockedCompareExchange(&g_itHeld.ready, 0, 0))
             + " globalsState=" + N((long long)g_p105G.state) + " (0 unread, 1 read, -1 refused)";
    }
    if (v == "square")   /* READ-ONLY: what this game shows at one square of a container (no window needed) */
    {
        if (tok.size() != 5) return usage;
        int x = 0, y = 0;
        if (P105Int(tok[3], 0, 999, &x) == 0 || P105Int(tok[4], 0, 999, &y) == 0) return "error cursortest square: x and y must be whole numbers 0..999";
        std::string desc;
        ::Inventory* inv = P105Container(tok[1], &desc);
        if (inv == 0) return "error cursortest square: " + desc;
        ::InventorySection* sec = inv->getSection(tok[2]);
        if (!ItObj(sec)) return "error cursortest square: " + desc + " has no section called '" + tok[2] + "'";
        if (ItSlotInSectionWhy(sec, x, y) != 1) return "error cursortest square: " + tok[2] + " has no square " + N((long long)x) + "," + N((long long)y);
        void* at = 0;
        if (ItGetAtPod(sec, x, y, &at) == 0) return "error cursortest square: the read faulted";
        return "ok cursortest square " + desc + " " + tok[2] + " " + N((long long)x) + "," + N((long long)y) + " holds " + P105ItemDesc(at) + " (read-only)";
    }
    if (v == "open")
    {
        if (tok.size() != 2) return usage;
        if (kShowTradeWindowRva == 0 || kCloseInventoriesRva == 0 || orig_showInventory == 0) return "error cursortest open: the loot open / close calls are not installed";
        if (cur0 != 0 || ItParityCursorBusy() != 0) return "error cursortest open: something is on the cursor - an open closes every window, and a close can destroy a cursor item";
        if (g_boxOpenState != 0) return "error cursortest open: a boxopen run is still going";
        void* b = ItBoxResolve(tok[1].c_str());
        if (b == 0) return "error cursortest open: no loaded box has the key " + tok[1];
        ::Character* opener = ItBoxOpenOpener();
        if (opener == 0) return "error cursortest open: no player-faction character with a uid this game owns";
        if (g_p105HaveTown == 0 && ItSaveTownHand(g_p105Town) != 0) g_p105HaveTown = 1;
        const int called = ItOpenLootWindow((void*)opener, b);
        ::Inventory* inv = ItBoxInventory(b);
        const int shown = (inv != 0 && P105WindowOf(inv) != 0) ? 1 : 0;
        if (called == 0 || shown == 0) return "error cursortest open box '" + tok[1] + "' (verdict " + N((long long)ItBoxMoveVerdict(b, tok[1])) + "): called=" + N((long long)called) + " windowShown=" + N((long long)shown);
        return "ok cursortest open box '" + tok[1] + "' (verdict " + N((long long)ItBoxMoveVerdict(b, tok[1])) + ") opener uid " + N((long long)FindSpawnedUid(opener))
             + " windowShown=1 (the engine's loot open; showInventory's detour asks the box's holder as in play)";
    }
    if (v == "close")
    {
        if (tok.size() != 1) return usage;
        if (cur0 != 0 || ItParityCursorBusy() != 0) return "error cursortest close: something is on the cursor - a close can destroy it (cursortest back first)";
        const int called = ItCloseAllInventories();
        int town = -1;
        if (g_p105HaveTown != 0) { town = ItRestoreTownHand(g_p105Town); g_p105HaveTown = 0; }
        if (called == 0) return "error cursortest close: closeAllInventories could not be called";
        return "ok cursortest close: every inventory window closed (town hand restored=" + N((long long)town) + ")";
    }
    if (v == "back")
    {
        if (tok.size() != 1) return usage;
        if (cur0 == 0) return "error cursortest back: nothing is on the cursor";
        if (kMouseReturnItemRva == 0 || kMouseInvPtrRva == 0) return "error cursortest back: the return row is not bound";
        const std::string was = P105ItemDesc(cur0);
        const int called = P105ReturnPod();
        void* const cur1 = ItHeldLive();
        ++g_p105Backs;
        if (called == 0 || cur1 != 0) return "error cursortest back: " + was + " called=" + N((long long)called) + " cursorAfter=" + P105ItemDesc(cur1);
        return "ok cursortest back: " + was + " put back by the engine's own return (MouseInventory::returnItem) cursorAfter=empty";
    }
    if (v == "pick")
    {
        int all = 0;
        if (tok.size() == 6 && tok[5] == "all") all = 1;
        else if (tok.size() != 5) return usage;
        if (cur0 != 0) return "error cursortest pick: something is already on the cursor (" + P105ItemDesc(cur0) + ")";
        ::Inventory* inv = 0; void* gui = 0; ::InventorySection* sec = 0;
        int x = 0, y = 0, left = 0, top = 0, sw = 0, sh = 0;
        std::string desc;
        const std::string bad = P105Aim(tok, "pick", &inv, &gui, &sec, &x, &y, &left, &top, &sw, &sh, &desc);
        if (!bad.empty()) return bad;
        void* before = 0;
        if (ItGetAtPod(sec, x, y, &before) == 0 || !ItObj(before)) return "error cursortest pick: nothing at " + tok[2] + " " + N((long long)x) + "," + N((long long)y) + " of " + desc;
        const std::string beforeDesc = P105ItemDesc(before);
        const int px = left + x * sw + sw / 2, py = top + y * sh + sh / 2;   /* the pickup TRUNCATES (its cvttss2si + idiv, checked by P105GlobalsOk): the centre is safe there */
        int pickFits = 0;
        const std::string premise = P105Premise(sec, before, x, y, 0, &pickFits);
        int pickRangeOk = -1;   /* T816: a box source reports how far the opener stands from it (report only; the pick is not refused) */
        const std::string pickRange = (tok[1] != "me" && tok[1] != "peer") ? P105RangeField(gui, (void*)ItBoxOpenOpener(), &pickRangeOk) : std::string();
        if (sw <= 0 || sh <= 0 || (px - left) / sw != x || (py - top) / sh != y)
            return "error cursortest pick: AIM CHECK FAILED - pixel " + N(px) + "," + N(py) + " grid=" + N(left) + "," + N(top) + " slot=" + N(sw) + "x" + N(sh)
                 + " does not convert back to " + N(x) + "," + N(y) + "; nothing called";
        P105StrPod s; P105MakeStr(&s, tok[2]);
        int r = -1;
        const int called = P105PickPod(gui, &s, (float)px, (float)py, all, &r);
        void* const cur1 = ItHeldLive();
        void* after = 0;
        ItGetAtPod(sec, x, y, &after);
        ++g_p105Picks;
        const std::string line = desc + " " + tok[2] + " " + N((long long)x) + "," + N((long long)y) + " mode=" + (all != 0 ? "all" : "one")
                               + " before=" + beforeDesc + " pixel=" + N((long long)px) + "," + N((long long)py) + " engine=" + N((long long)r)
                               + " cursor=" + P105ItemDesc(cur1) + (cur1 == before ? " (the same object)" : (cur1 != 0 ? " (a split-off copy)" : ""))
                               + " squareNow=" + P105ItemDesc(after) + " heldSlot=" + N((long long)::InterlockedCompareExchange(&g_itHeld.ready, 0, 0))
                               + " fixture:" + premise + pickRange;
        if (called == 0) return "error cursortest pick FAULTED " + line;
        if (cur1 == 0) return "error cursortest pick: the engine's pickup lifted nothing - " + line;
        g_p105PickWho = tok[1]; g_p105PickSec = tok[2]; g_p105PickItem = cur1;
        return "ok cursortest pick " + line;
    }
    if (v == "drop")
    {
        /* `free` in place of x y: the first square of that section the engine would take the carried item at (ItFirstFreeSlot) */
        const int dropFree = (tok.size() == 4 && tok[3] == "free") ? 1 : 0;
        if (tok.size() != 5 && dropFree == 0) return usage;
        if (cur0 == 0) return "error cursortest drop: nothing is on the cursor";
        std::vector<std::string> aim(tok);
        if (dropFree != 0) { aim[3] = "0"; aim.push_back("0"); }
        ::Inventory* inv = 0; void* gui = 0; ::InventorySection* sec = 0;
        int x = 0, y = 0, left = 0, top = 0, sw = 0, sh = 0;
        std::string desc;
        const std::string bad = P105Aim(aim, "drop", &inv, &gui, &sec, &x, &y, &left, &top, &sw, &sh, &desc);
        if (!bad.empty()) return bad;
        if (dropFree != 0 && (ItFirstFreeSlot(sec, cur0, &x, &y) == 0 || x < 0 || y < 0))
            return "error cursortest drop: " + desc + " " + tok[2] + " has no free square for " + P105ItemDesc(cur0);
        const std::string carried = P105ItemDesc(cur0);
        int fits = 0;
        const std::string premise = P105Premise(sec, cur0, x, y, 1, &fits);
        int rangeOk = -1;   /* T816: 0x714990's first check (0x70C6C0) - the cursor's source owner must stand within range of the target */
        const std::string rangeF = P105RangeField(gui, 0, &rangeOk);
        const int px = left + x * sw + sw / 4, py = top + y * sh + sh / 4;   /* a quarter in from the square's top-left (see the block comment) */
        std::string aimFields;
        const std::string aimBad = P105AimCheck(sec, px, py, left, top, sw, sh, x, y, &aimFields);
        const std::string head = desc + " " + tok[2] + " " + N(x) + "," + N(y) + " carried=" + carried + " pixel=" + N(px) + "," + N(py)
                               + aimFields + " fixture:" + premise + rangeF;
        if (!aimBad.empty())
            return "error cursortest drop: AIM CHECK FAILED - " + aimBad + "; nothing called, the item stays on the cursor (cursortest back) - " + head;
        if (fits != 1)
            return "error cursortest drop: PREMISE FAILED - the square does not take the carried item (fits=" + N(fits) + ": see limitedTo / enabled /"
                   " square / sizes); nothing called, the item stays on the cursor (cursortest back) - " + head;
        if (rangeOk == 0)   /* T816: the engine would refuse at its first check (T813: 1,596 units) - refused here, before the engine call */
            return "error cursortest drop: PREMISE FAILED" + rangeF + "; nothing called, the item stays on the cursor (cursortest back) - " + head;
        /* T818: the 0x710B70 flag, the range test with it, the silent-gate reads - only now, after the aim and premise checks passed:
           0x710B70 is look-up-or-create, so a drop the lever refuses never touches the engine's table */
        const std::string gateF = P105GateFields(gui, sec);
        P105InstallMsgHook();   /* T818 review: the reason hook, installed on the first drop that gets here (once; remembered) */
        P105StrPod s; P105MakeStr(&s, tok[2]);
        int r = -1;
        g_p105MsgCode = 0; g_p105MsgCount = 0;
        ::InterlockedExchange(&g_p105MsgArm, 1);   /* T818: detour_p105Msg remembers the code the engine shows during this one call */
        const int called = P105PlacePod(gui, &s, px, py, &r);
        ::InterlockedExchange(&g_p105MsgArm, 0);
        const std::string reason = (g_p105MsgHook != 1) ? std::string(" engineReason=unhooked")
            : (g_p105MsgCount == 0) ? std::string(" engineReason=none")
            : " engineReason=" + N((long long)g_p105MsgCode) + ":" + P105ReasonText(g_p105MsgCode) + (g_p105MsgCount > 1 ? " messages=" + N((long long)g_p105MsgCount) : std::string(""));
        void* const cur1 = ItHeldLive();
        void* now = 0;
        ItGetAtPod(sec, x, y, &now);
        ++g_p105Drops;
        int tx = -1, ty = -1;
        const std::string where = P105WhereIs(cur0, cur1, sec, &tx, &ty);
        const std::string line = head + gateF + " engine=" + N(r) + reason + " now=" + where + " squareNow=" + P105ItemDesc(now) + (now != 0 && now == cur0 ? " (the carried object)" : "")
                               + " cursorAfter=" + P105ItemDesc(cur1) + (cur1 != 0 && cur1 != cur0 ? " (another item is on the cursor now)" : "");
        if (called == 0) return "error cursortest drop FAULTED " + line;
        if (r == 1 && tx == x && ty == y && cur1 == 0) return "ok cursortest drop " + line + " - the engine placed it in the wanted square";
        if (r == 1) return "error cursortest drop: the engine answered 1 but the carried object is not alone in the wanted square - " + line;
        const std::string gates = " (engineReason= is the code the engine showed through the refusal-message function during the call; none = one of its silent put-backs: the footprint, the count cap (capFull=), the section type list)";
        if (cur0 != 0 && ItHeldLive() == cur0)   /* the engine refused and left it on the cursor: the lever's own back */
        {
            const int backCalled = P105ReturnPod();
            ++g_p105Backs;
            void* const cur2 = ItHeldLive();
            int bx = -1, by = -1;
            const std::string w2 = P105WhereIs(cur0, cur2, sec, &bx, &by);
            return "error cursortest drop: ENGINE REFUSED (engine=" + N(r) + ") - " + line + "; it stayed on the cursor, so the lever ran cursortest back: called="
                 + N(backCalled) + " now=" + w2 + " cursorAfter=" + P105ItemDesc(cur2) + gates;
        }
        return "error cursortest drop: ENGINE REFUSED (engine=" + N(r) + ") - " + line + "; the engine put it back itself (its refusals call 0x70D000), no lever back needed" + gates;
    }
    return usage;
}
/* T-159 TEST-ONLY: boxmove <fromKey> <section> <fx> <fy> <toKey> [n] - n units (the whole item when omitted or >= its count) from one
   square of a box into the FIRST FREE square of the same-named section of ANOTHER box, through the engine's own take-out + add, so the
   drain sees a one-tick move between two boxes. */
std::string P105BoxMoveCross(const std::vector<std::string>& tok)
{
    int fx = 0, fy = 0, n = 0;
    if (P105Int(tok[2], 0, 999, &fx) == 0 || P105Int(tok[3], 0, 999, &fy) == 0) return "error boxmove: the squares must be whole numbers 0..999";
    if (tok.size() == 6 && P105Int(tok[5], 1, 100000, &n) == 0) return "error boxmove: n must be a whole number 1..100000";
    void* b = ItBoxResolve(tok[0].c_str());
    if (b == 0) return "error boxmove: no loaded box has the key " + tok[0];
    void* b2 = ItBoxResolve(tok[4].c_str());
    if (b2 == 0) return "error boxmove: no loaded box has the key " + tok[4];
    if (b == b2) return "error boxmove: both keys name the same box (use <tx> <ty> for a move inside one box)";
    ::Inventory* inv = ItBoxInventory(b);
    ::Inventory* inv2 = ItBoxInventory(b2);
    if (inv == 0 || inv2 == 0) return "error boxmove: box '" + (inv == 0 ? tok[0] : tok[4]) + "' has no readable inventory";
    const int v1 = ItBoxMoveVerdict(b, tok[0]), v2 = ItBoxMoveVerdict(b2, tok[4]);
    ::InventorySection* sec = inv->getSection(tok[1]);
    ::InventorySection* sec2 = inv2->getSection(tok[1]);
    if (!ItObj(sec) || !ItObj(sec2)) return "error boxmove: box '" + (!ItObj(sec) ? tok[0] : tok[4]) + "' has no section called '" + tok[1] + "'";
    if (ItSlotInSectionWhy(sec, fx, fy) != 1) return "error boxmove: " + tok[1] + " has no such square";
    void* item = 0;
    if (ItGetAtPod(sec, fx, fy, &item) == 0 || !ItObj(item)) return "error boxmove: nothing at " + tok[1] + " " + N((long long)fx) + "," + N((long long)fy);
    int q0 = 0;
    ItIntPod(item, kItemQuantity, &q0);
    const std::string before = P105ItemDesc(item);
    int tx = -1, ty = -1;
    if (ItFirstFreeSlot(sec2, item, &tx, &ty) != 1 || tx < 0) return "error boxmove: box '" + tok[4] + "' has no free square for " + before + " - nothing moved";
    const int split = (n > 0 && n < q0) ? 1 : 0;
    void* moved = 0;
    const int tookCall = ItTakeOutPod(inv, item, split != 0 ? n : -1, &moved);
    if (tookCall == 0 || !ItObj(moved))
        return "error boxmove: the engine's take-out " + std::string(tookCall == 0 ? "faulted" : "gave nothing") + " - " + before;
    const int placed = ItLeverAddAt(sec2, moved, tx, ty);
    if (placed == -1) { ++g_testLeverAddFaulted; return "error boxmove: the engine's add FAULTED; the item is kept where that left it (" + P105ItemDesc(moved) + ")"; }
    if (placed != 1)
    {
        if (split == 0)
        {
            const int back = ItLeverPutBackAt(sec, moved, fx, fy);
            if (back == 1) ++g_leverPutBack; else ++g_leverLost;
            return "error boxmove: box '" + tok[4] + "' took nothing at " + N((long long)tx) + "," + N((long long)ty) + "; put back at the source=" + N((long long)back);
        }
        int rx = -1, ry = -1, alt = 0;
        if (ItFirstFreeSlot(sec, moved, &rx, &ry) != 0 && rx >= 0) alt = ItLeverAddAt(sec, moved, rx, ry);
        if (alt != 1) ++g_leverLost;
        return "error boxmove: the split-off " + P105ItemDesc(moved) + " was refused by box '" + tok[4] + "'; placed back in the source box at "
             + N((long long)rx) + "," + N((long long)ry) + " = " + N((long long)alt) + (alt != 1 ? " - LOST (leverLost +1)" : "");
    }
    ++g_p105Moves;
    void* src = 0;
    ItGetAtPod(sec, fx, fy, &src);
    return "ok boxmove box '" + tok[0] + "' (verdict " + N((long long)v1) + ") " + tok[1] + " " + N((long long)fx) + "," + N((long long)fy) + " -> box '" + tok[4]
         + "' (verdict " + N((long long)v2) + ") " + tok[1] + " " + N((long long)tx) + "," + N((long long)ty) + " " + (split != 0 ? "split n=" + N((long long)n) : std::string("whole"))
         + " before=" + before + " moved=" + P105ItemDesc(moved) + " sourceNow=" + P105ItemDesc(src)
         + " - the engine's own take-out + add rang (two boxes); the drain sees them this tick";
}
std::string P105BoxMoveBody(const std::string& arg)
{
    const std::vector<std::string> tok = P105Tokens(arg);
    const std::string usage = "error boxmove usage: boxmove <boxKey> <section> <fx> <fy> <tx> <ty> [n] | boxmove <fromKey> <section> <fx> <fy> <toKey> [n]";
    const int cross = ((tok.size() == 5 || tok.size() == 6) && tok[4].find('@') != std::string::npos) ? 1 : 0;   /* a box key always carries '@' */
    if (tok.size() != 6 && tok.size() != 7 && cross == 0) return usage;
    if (g_base == 0) return "error boxmove: not installed";
    if (ItOnMainThread() == 0) return "error boxmove: not on the main thread";
    if (StoreTearingDown() != 0) return "error boxmove: the engine is tearing the world down - try again";
    if (ItParityCursorBusy() != 0 || ItHeldLive() != 0) return "error boxmove: something is on the cursor";
    if (cross != 0) return P105BoxMoveCross(tok);
    int fx = 0, fy = 0, tx = 0, ty = 0, n = 0;
    if (P105Int(tok[2], 0, 999, &fx) == 0 || P105Int(tok[3], 0, 999, &fy) == 0 || P105Int(tok[4], 0, 999, &tx) == 0 || P105Int(tok[5], 0, 999, &ty) == 0)
        return "error boxmove: the squares must be whole numbers 0..999";
    if (tok.size() == 7 && P105Int(tok[6], 1, 100000, &n) == 0) return "error boxmove: n must be a whole number 1..100000";
    if (fx == tx && fy == ty) return "error boxmove: the two squares are the same";
    void* b = ItBoxResolve(tok[0].c_str());
    if (b == 0) return "error boxmove: no loaded box has the key " + tok[0];
    ::Inventory* inv = ItBoxInventory(b);
    if (inv == 0) return "error boxmove: box '" + tok[0] + "' has no readable inventory";
    const int verdict = ItBoxMoveVerdict(b, tok[0]);
    ::InventorySection* sec = inv->getSection(tok[1]);
    if (!ItObj(sec)) return "error boxmove: box '" + tok[0] + "' has no section called '" + tok[1] + "'";
    if (ItSlotInSectionWhy(sec, fx, fy) != 1 || ItSlotInSectionWhy(sec, tx, ty) != 1) return "error boxmove: " + tok[1] + " has no such square";
    void* item = 0;
    if (ItGetAtPod(sec, fx, fy, &item) == 0 || !ItObj(item)) return "error boxmove: nothing at " + tok[1] + " " + N((long long)fx) + "," + N((long long)fy);
    int q0 = 0;
    ItIntPod(item, kItemQuantity, &q0);
    const std::string before = P105ItemDesc(item);
    void* occ = 0;
    ItGetAtPod(sec, tx, ty, &occ);
    if (occ != 0) return "error boxmove: the square " + N((long long)tx) + "," + N((long long)ty) + " holds " + P105ItemDesc(occ) + " - this lever moves into a free square only";
    if (ItFitsPod(sec, item, tx, ty) != 1) return "error boxmove: the engine would not take " + before + " at " + N((long long)tx) + "," + N((long long)ty) + " - nothing moved";
    const int split = (n > 0 && n < q0) ? 1 : 0;
    const long long sent0 = g_reqSent;
    void* moved = 0;
    const int tookCall = ItTakeOutPod(inv, item, split != 0 ? n : -1, &moved);
    if (tookCall == 0 || !ItObj(moved))
        return "error boxmove: the engine's take-out " + std::string(tookCall == 0 ? "faulted" : "gave nothing") + " - " + before;
    const int placed = ItLeverAddAt(sec, moved, tx, ty);
    if (placed == -1) { ++g_testLeverAddFaulted; return "error boxmove: the engine's add FAULTED; the item is kept where that left it (" + P105ItemDesc(moved) + ")"; }
    if (placed != 1)
    {
        if (split == 0)
        {
            const int back = ItLeverPutBackAt(sec, moved, fx, fy);
            if (back == 1) ++g_leverPutBack; else ++g_leverLost;
            return "error boxmove: the destination square took nothing; put back at the source=" + N((long long)back);
        }
        int rx = -1, ry = -1, alt = 0;
        if (ItFirstFreeSlot(sec, moved, &rx, &ry) != 0 && rx >= 0) alt = ItLeverAddAt(sec, moved, rx, ry);
        if (alt != 1) ++g_leverLost;
        return "error boxmove: the split-off " + P105ItemDesc(moved) + " was refused at " + N((long long)tx) + "," + N((long long)ty)
             + "; placed at the first free square " + N((long long)rx) + "," + N((long long)ry) + " = " + N((long long)alt) + (alt != 1 ? " - LOST (leverLost +1)" : "");
    }
    ++g_p105Moves;
    void* src = 0;
    ItGetAtPod(sec, fx, fy, &src);
    return "ok boxmove box '" + tok[0] + "' (verdict " + N((long long)verdict) + ") " + tok[1] + " " + N((long long)fx) + "," + N((long long)fy) + " -> "
         + N((long long)tx) + "," + N((long long)ty) + " " + (split != 0 ? "split n=" + N((long long)n) : std::string("whole")) + " before=" + before
         + " moved=" + P105ItemDesc(moved) + " sourceNow=" + P105ItemDesc(src) + " - the engine's own take-out + add rang; the drain sees them this tick"
           " (reqSent before=" + N(sent0) + ")";
}
} // namespace (p105h)
std::string CursorTestCommand(const std::string& arg)
{
    const std::string r = P105CursorBody(arg);
    if (r.compare(0, 3, "ok ") == 0) DebugLog("[ITEMS] p105 " + r.substr(3));
    else { ++g_p105Refused; DebugLog("[ITEMS] p105 cursortest REFUSED args='" + arg + "': " + r); }
    return r;
}
std::string BoxMoveCommand(const std::string& arg)
{
    const std::string r = P105BoxMoveBody(arg);
    if (r.compare(0, 3, "ok ") == 0) DebugLog("[ITEMS] p105 " + r.substr(3));
    else { ++g_p105Refused; DebugLog("[ITEMS] p105 boxmove REFUSED args='" + arg + "': " + r); }
    return r;
}
